  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#47\", \"PowerToys#23312\", \"PowerToys#4043\"], \"answer\": \"This feature has been requested before. PowerToys#47 is the main tracking issue for minimizing to the tray by right-clicking the minimize button. The team closed #23312 and #4043 as duplicates of #47, so add your +1 and your use case there. The archive shows no sign that PowerToys has built this feature, and I found no ticket saying it is planned. Until it exists, the tickets point to third-party tools. RBTray (https://github.com/[user]/rbtray) does exactly this, but users report it doesn't work with every app, for example Opera. Also, PowerToys#18015 reports that RBTray's hook stopped the PowerToys Settings app from loading, so close RBTray or run it with `--no-hook` if that happens. Another option is the AutoHotkey-based Min2Tray (https://junyx.breadfan.de/Min2Tray/).\"}",
